  "unit_interface": "Push depth+1 and pop depth\u22121 carry odd transverse residues. Zero-height packet edges carry even residue, possibly2, not necessarily0. Private chains preserve exact whole-packet transverse displacement modulo4 and put the full packet C count on their first unit edge.",
  "initial_transverse_parity": "A port at depthd has exact headheightq=\u221218\u2212d. Its two admitted initial residues are t in{0,1,2,3} with t\u2261q modulo2; equivalently q and t have the same physical checker parity. All initial lowhead heights are quantified, not stack-capped. Initial high tokens are absent and retained ages mature, so only low-prefix reachability is used.",
  "port_format": "RESIDUE_PORTS NP NE NI 4; initial IDs; NP rows(heading,DFA,depth); NE rows(source,target,delta_t_mod4,max_saturated_C_FOR_THAT_RESIDUE). Unmatched pop/push segments retain all4 residues. Maximum weights are never shared across distinct transverse residues.",
  "scope": "Exact weighted packet-DFA low-counter relaxation summaries, finite derivation certificates and full port projection controls. No unretained low-cell color legality, complete record model, record exclusion or capture theorem is claimed.",
